              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "Opioids are a broad class of drugs used primarily for pain relief. Depending on how they are made, they are derived from either the **opium poppy plant (*Papaver somniferum*)** or created synthetically in a laboratory to mimic the plant's natural compounds. \n\nTo understand what they are derived from, opioids are generally categorized into three main groups based on their origin:\n\n### 1. Natural Opioids (Opiates)\nThese are organic compounds derived directly from the **milky sap (latex)** found in the unripe seed pods of the opium poppy plant. Historically, only these naturally occurring plant extracts were called \"opiates\".\n*   **How they are harvested:** When the poppy seed pod is lightly sliced, a white, sticky sap oozes out. When dried, this sap becomes raw opium.\n*   **Examples:** \n    *   **Morphine** (the primary active ingredient in opium)\n    *   **Codeine**\n    *   **Thebaine** (a minor alkaloid used primarily as a starting material to make other drugs)\n\n### 2. Semi-Synthetic Opioids\nThese drugs are created in a laboratory by **chemically modifying natural opiates**. Scientists take natural compounds extracted from the poppy plant (like morphine or thebaine) and alter their chemical structures to make them stronger, longer-lasting, or faster-acting.\n*   **Examples:**\n    *   **Oxycodone** (OxyContin, Percocet) \u2013 derived from thebaine\n    *   **Hydrocodone** (Vicodin) \u2013 synthesized from codeine or thebaine\n    *   **Heroin** \u2013 chemically synthesized from morphine\n    *   **Hydromorphone** (Dilaudid) \u2013 derived from morphine\n\n### 3. Fully Synthetic Opioids\nThese are entirely **man-made in chemical laboratories**. They do not contain any plant material from the opium poppy. Instead, chemists design these synthetic molecules from scratch to mimic the exact molecular shape of natural opiates, allowing them to bind to the same pain receptors in the human brain and nervous system.\n*   **Examples:**\n    *   **Fentanyl** (highly potent, synthesized entirely from laboratory precursor chemicals)\n    *   **Methadone**\n    *   **Tramadol** \n\n### Summary\nWhile **natural and semi-synthetic opioids** rely on the **opium poppy plant** as their base ingredient, **synthetic opioids** are built entirely from **artificial chemicals** in a lab to reproduce the same pain-relieving and euphoric effects.",
